description: A simple guide to cooking eggs various ways in a Sub-Zero Wolf steam oven.
---

= All Recipes =

@Eggs, @Kosher Salt{}, @Black Pepper{}, @Oil

#ramekins{4}

= Hard-Boiled Eggs =

Place desired number of whole eggs directly on a wire rack in the middle of the convection steam oven. 

Set the oven to Steam mode at 210°F and cook for ~{20%minutes} for hard-boiled eggs.
After cooking, transfer eggs to an ice bath for ~{5%minutes} before peeling.

= Scrambled Eggs =

In a medium bowl, beat desired number of eggs; season with salt and pepper.
Pour contents into a vacuum-seal or zip-top bag, then close securely.

Place bag on the perforated pan in the middle of the convection steam oven.
Set the oven to Steam mode at 210°F and cook for ~{5%minutes}.
Remove the bag and shake it well to break the egg mixture into pieces.
Return the bag to the oven and cook for an additional ~{2%minutes} or until eggs are cooked to your desired donneness.

= Sunny-Side Steamed =

Lightly grease desired number of small ceramic or stoneware plates or saucers with non-stick spray, butter, or oil.
Crack one egg onto each dish.

Place the dishes on a wire rack in the middle of the convection steam oven.
Set the oven to Steam mode at 210°F and cook for ~{5%minutes} or until eggs are cooked to your desired doneness.

= Steam Poached =

Lightly grease desired number of small ceramic or stoneware ramekins with non-stick spray, butter, or oil.
Crack one egg into each ramekin.
Swirl the ramekin until the yolk rests in the middle of the dish; the yolk should not rest against the side of the dish.
Cover each ramekin with plastic wrap.

Place the ramekins on a wire rack in the middle of the convection steam oven.
Set the oven to Steam mode at 185°F and cook for ~{13%minutes} or until eggs are cooked to your desired doneness (see notes).

Remove one ramekin from the oven and gently shake it; ensure the whites are set and fully cooked.
If undercooked whites remain, continue steaming at 1-minute intervals.

Onece the eggs are fully cooked, remove the tray and ramekins from the oven.
Let eggs rest, covered, for ~{1%minute} before serving.

Approximate cook times: 12 minutes for very runny yolk and almost undercooked whites;
13 minutes for over easy runny tolk;
15-16 minutes for medium slightly runny yolk;
18-20 minutes for fully set custardy yolk;
25-30 minutes for fully set yolk and whites.

= Breakfast Sandwich =

Lightly grease four 6-oz ramekins with non-stick spray, butter, or oil.

Either beat four eggs together before dividing evely between the dishes,
or crack one egg into each ramekin leaving the yolk intact.
Season with salt and pepper.

Place the ramekins on a wire rack in the middle of the convection steam oven.
Set the oven to Steam mode at 200°F and cook for ~{7%minutes} or until eggs are cooked to your desired doneness.

Carefully remove the ramekins from the oven. Using a fork, gently loosen and remove the eggs.

Place the eggs on @English Muffins{4}(toasted) or @Bagels{4}(toasted).
Optionally top with @Cheese{4%slices}, @Avocado{1}(sliced), @Tomato{1}(sliced),
@Breakfast Sausage{4%patties}(cooked), or @Bacon{4%slices}(cooked).
